{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1795108720,"nonce":"0BJXK9DhVLnz+rsPekFqO/GZRQo=","title":"PARKED: pack session mutex serializes a fence's durable PUTs; measure drain time first","was":"Every durable PUT of a fence serializes on the pack session's tokio Mutex, held across PackWriter::append -\u003e put_part (an 8 MiB part upload). The drain client's buffer_unordered(16) therefore collapses to ~one sequential S3 stream on the pack leg. This partially re-introduces the per-request cost on the leg ADR-0061 measured at 81-88% of a Step boundary — invisibly, because nothing fails."}]}